<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-01T22:08:57+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 01 Sep 2026 22:08:57 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[A Staten Island deli manager started paying kids for better report cards 3 years ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133686923.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A deli manager on Staten Island has sparked a remarkable movement by rewarding children for their academic achievements. This initiative has successfully gathered an impressive $500,000 to procure school supplies, benefiting numerous students. Thousands received fully stocked backpacks just in time for the new school year, showcasing how community backing can elevate a simple idea into a significant educational support system.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-staten-island-deli-manager-started-paying-kids-for-better-report-cards-3-years-ago-his-fundraiser-has-now-crossed-500000-and-he-is-giving-school-supplies-to-3000-students/articleshow/133686923.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-staten-island-deli-manager-started-paying-kids-for-better-report-cards-3-years-ago-his-fundraiser-has-now-crossed-500000-and-he-is-giving-school-supplies-to-3000-students/articleshow/133686923.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T22:02:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133687266,imgsize-988208.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2023, buyers paid $87,000 for a crumbling 1979 Michigan concrete dome with caved-in ceilings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133686236.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Brighton, Michigan, a remarkable transformation has taken place with a once-neglected 1970s concrete dome home. Acquired in 2023 for $87,000, this property underwent a meticulous renovation, now boasting four bedrooms infused with modern luxury and eco-friendly features. Now on the market for $499,900, its unique design and energy-efficient qualities are captivating buyers in search of distinctive living spaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2023-buyers-paid-87000-for-a-crumbling-1979-michigan-concrete-dome-with-caved-in-ceilings-after-a-total-overhaul-the-2457-sq-ft-home-is-back-for-499900/articleshow/133686236.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2023-buyers-paid-87000-for-a-crumbling-1979-michigan-concrete-dome-with-caved-in-ceilings-after-a-total-overhaul-the-2457-sq-ft-home-is-back-for-499900/articleshow/133686236.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T21:17:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133686361,imgsize-1941871.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 19-year-old's girlfriend fell onto train tracks; he jumped down to save her and died after...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133685691.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A nineteen-year-old man lost his life in a tragic act of courage while on his first subway journey. He leaped onto the tracks after his girlfriend stumbled, attempting to save her. Unfortunately, he came into contact with the electric third rail. Now in critical condition, his girlfriend is hospitalized, spurring urgent calls for better safety measures on subway platforms.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-19-year-old-was-taking-a-boston-train-for-the-first-time-when-his-girlfriend-fell-onto-the-tracks-he-jumped-down-to-save-her-and-died-after-hitting-the-electrified-third-rail/articleshow/133685691.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-19-year-old-was-taking-a-boston-train-for-the-first-time-when-his-girlfriend-fell-onto-the-tracks-he-jumped-down-to-save-her-and-died-after-hitting-the-electrified-third-rail/articleshow/133685691.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T20:37:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133685747,imgsize-598047.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1944, Polish priest Henry Denis endured Nazi malaria experiments at Dachau; after surviving he...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133681630.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Father Henry J. Denis emerged from the horrors of Dachau concentration camp and the inhumane medical experiments conducted there. With a steadfast vow to create a shrine to Mary if he survived, he eventually settled in Nebraska, where he honored that promise. The Our Lady of Fatima Shrine, dedicated in August 1956, serves as a powerful symbol of hope and unwavering faith transcending time and geography.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1944-polish-priest-henry-denis-endured-nazi-malaria-experiments-at-dachau-after-surviving-the-camp-he-fulfilled-his-vow-by-building-our-lady-of-fatima-shrine-in-nebraska/articleshow/133681630.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1944-polish-priest-henry-denis-endured-nazi-malaria-experiments-at-dachau-after-surviving-the-camp-he-fulfilled-his-vow-by-building-our-lady-of-fatima-shrine-in-nebraska/articleshow/133681630.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T20:25:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133685437,imgsize-2248676.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[WWII-era plane packed into boxes in 1953 moved with its owner for 50 years before restoration]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133652923.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The WACO UPF-7 was used as a primary trainer from 1941, helping prepare pilots through the US government-backed Civilian Pilot Training Program during the World War II era. Retired in 1953, the aircraft was bought by a Florida owner who dismantled and packed it into boxes, carrying the parts through three moves over 50 years. Rediscovered in 2002, it was later restored by RARE Aircraft and returned to airworthy condition before being displayed at the Historic Flight Foundation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wwii-era-training-plane-was-packed-into-boxes-in-1953-its-owner-carried-the-pieces-through-3-moves-for-50-years-before-the-forgotten-aircraft-was-finally-restored/articleshow/133652923.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wwii-era-training-plane-was-packed-into-boxes-in-1953-its-owner-carried-the-pieces-through-3-moves-for-50-years-before-the-forgotten-aircraft-was-finally-restored/articleshow/133652923.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T19:55:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133653924,imgsize-134518.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1943, two Jewish refugees bought a LA mansion for $9,000; 83 yrs later, Villa Aurora has reopened]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133647979.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Villa Aurora, a historic mansion in Pacific Palisades, has reopened after restoration work following the January 2025 Palisades Fire. The house was bought in 1943 for $9,000 by German Jewish writer Lion Feuchtwanger and his wife Marta, who had fled Nazi persecution. It later became a gathering place for artists and intellectuals and an international artist residency.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1943-two-jewish-refugees-fleeing-the-nazis-bought-a-crumbling-los-angeles-mansion-for-9000-83-years-later-after-the-palisades-fire-forced-it-shut-villa-aurora-has-reopened/articleshow/133647979.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1943-two-jewish-refugees-fleeing-the-nazis-bought-a-crumbling-los-angeles-mansion-for-9000-83-years-later-after-the-palisades-fire-forced-it-shut-villa-aurora-has-reopened/articleshow/133647979.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T19:55:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133649175,imgsize-128221.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Israeli PM Netanyahu’s son urgently evacuated from US over ‘significant threat’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133685475.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/israeli-pm-netanyahus-son-urgently-evacuated-from-us-over-significant-threat/articleshow/133685475.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/israeli-pm-netanyahus-son-urgently-evacuated-from-us-over-significant-threat/articleshow/133685475.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T20:29:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133685508,imgsize-77263.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1937, Pittsburgh built a 102-foot water tank that doubled as a park lookout]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662724.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The historic North Park Observation Tower in Pittsburgh is poised to reopen its doors after being closed for years. A comprehensive restoration effort is underway, focusing on the beloved 1937 building and its staircase, while also enhancing the surrounding park area with fresh landscaping and improved accessibility. Funded by a mix of public and private investments, the landmark is anticipated to welcome guests once more by 2027.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1937-pittsburgh-built-a-102-foot-water-tank-that-doubled-as-a-park-lookout-closed-for-decades-it-is-getting-a-3-million-restoration-to-reopen-its-154-step-climb-and-skyline-view/articleshow/133662724.